# Local env files must never reach a deployment.
#
# `vercel --prod` uploads the working directory, and it does not read
# .gitignore — so a gitignored .env still shipped, and Next.js loads .env in
# every environment. A local-only SMS_KILL_SWITCH=true rode along that way and
# silenced production texting until someone noticed nobody was being told they
# were on the clock.
#
# Production configuration belongs in Vercel's environment variables, which
# take precedence over these files anyway.
.env
.env.*
